Sounds like you have all of the sources of gold covered.  Gold gets
more common as you dig deeper.  Also a couple of the detect
scrolls will find gold embedded in rock.  Sometimes you dig there
and it isn't on your level so try a pit.

> * Other than protection and looking for random items, are there other
> good ways of reducing my AC without descending further?

Yes there are other ways.

> Enchant armor scripts have been very rare in this game.  So have shops.
>  Only 1 outside of Minetown.  So, I've been biding my time fighting
> ogres on the first quest level looking for enchant armor scrolls.

Make sure you try on ever b/u piece of armor looking for better
enchanted ones.  Pray holding as many cursed objects as you
can hold as one of the possible prayer benefits is uncursing
everything in your inventory then you have even more to try on.

If you can find a way to write scrolls it's easy to come by blank
ones.  Given water walking or magical breathing a pool gives
unlimited water compared to limited fountains.

If you've donated to more than one priest and you're out of
purchased protection use your charisma (in the form of a stack
of highly enchanted daggers and a few hundred arrows) to
consolidate the gold from all but one of them.

Since learning that protection AC is one of the benefits of
prayer I've given up on purchasing protection from priests.



